PKGCHECK_EXEC_RESULT_CODEC(3)

# NAME

encode_check_execution_result, decode_check_execution_result - retain and reopen exact native check-execution evidence

# SYNOPSIS

*#include <libpkgcheck-exec/result_codec.h>*

*check_execution_result_encoding encode_check_execution_result(const check_execution_result& result);*

*check_execution_result decode_check_execution_result(const check_execution_result_encoding& encoding, pkgcheck::check_request check_request, pkgexec::execution_request execution_request, pkgexec::backend_capability_profile backend);*

# DESCRIPTION

*encode_check_execution_result*() emits the canonical versioned record for one
retained *check_execution_result*. The record embeds the canonical
*libpkgexec* execution-result encoding and retains the corresponding terminal
check outcome, execution-evidence identity, failure classification,
failure-evidence identity, and check-result identity.

*decode_check_execution_result*() requires the exact check request, execution
request, and backend capability profile bodies. It verifies the whole-record
checksum, delegates subordinate execution evidence to *libpkgexec*, rebuilds
the terminal check result through its public factories, checks every retained
identity, and requires canonical byte-for-byte re-encoding.

The codec never serializes or reconstructs admitted sessions, source trees,
checked-package resources, package-input resources, host paths, credentials, execution
resources, or backend semantics. Identity strings are not semantic authority.
Decoding performs no tree discovery, backend invocation, program execution,
retry, progression publication, filesystem access, or mutation.

# ERRORS

Malformed, truncated, noncanonical, or internally inconsistent bytes raise
*pkgcheck_exec::error* with *corrupt_encoding*. A valid record presented with
a different check request, execution request, or backend profile raises
*authority_mismatch*. Encoding a result that violates the adapter contract
raises *inconsistent_result*.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgcheck-exec*(7), *pkgexec_result_codec*(3), *libpkgcheck*(3), *libpkgexec*(3)
